WEBVTT

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.050
<b>tsukinuketa aoi sora</b>

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.050
<b>The blue sky has broken through</b>

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>saa dekakeyou</b>

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>Come, let's go out</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.890
<b>itsumo no namikimichi jitensha wo koideku</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.890
<b>Riding my bike through the usual avenue</b>

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>ima sugu ni aitai yo</b>

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>"I want to meet you now."</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>omoi ga kaze wo kiri</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>That thought is blown away by the wind,</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>kimi e to hakondeku tegami ni natte</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>and becomes a letter being carried to you</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.350
<b>koko kara hajimaru monogatari fly!</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.350
<b>The story that starts from here... Fly!</b>

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>kawariyuku kisetsu ga ashioto wo tatetemo</b>

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:59.660
<b>Even if the changing seasons walk on with loud footsteps,</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.490
<b>sou kawaranai suki to iu tsubasa</b>

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:06.490
<b>the wings of love won't change</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.500
<b>dokomade mo tondeke oozora takaku</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.500
<b>Fly far away, high into the sky</b>

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:20.730
<b>koi no tenki yohou hare nochi hare ni nare</b>

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:20.730
<b>May the weather forecast of love be sunny and clear forever</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>ashita mo asatte mo</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.400
<b>Tomorrow and the day after tomorrow</b>

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:31.820
Rise!

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.700
<b>Episode 9    Cross the River of Time</b>

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.460
Bow!

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.550
Don't slack off now.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:36.790
I'm off!

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.160
He sure was in a hurry—

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.490
Oh, he had a date.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.090
This is no good.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:58.250
Kenji!

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:58.950
Yeah?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.450
That's "Yes, sir" you idiot.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:02.580
Yes, sir?

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.770
We're replacing all of these!

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.390
Take the shingles from me from below.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.740
Yes, Gen-san.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.210
A date, huh?

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.130
He was just meeting Gen-san.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.000
Ken-chan likes older people.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.180
Be careful, you idiot!

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.230
He's beaming!

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:18.870
Yes, sir!

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.080
What a relief, huh?

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.670
Time to go.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.900
We still have to write some fortune strips at home.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:34.980
Gen-san!

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.050
Gen-san, hold on!

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.970
Are you okay, Gen-san!?

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.430
Are you hurt?

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.070
We should probably go see a doctor—

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.000
Moron!

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.580
A hip will heal after resting for a day.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.170
See anything interesting?

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:01.930
Pretty big, huh?

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.570
It's called the Yamato.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:04.960
Yamato?

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.120
What's that?

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.500
The biggest battleship in the world.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.460
I used to serve on that ship.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:18.770
It was 1942. I must've been around 22 years old.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.800
I embarked with the 15th Construction Division,

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.160
riding all the way across Southeast Asia and the Pacific.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.900
It was such a beautiful ship.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:33.270
At first, I even wondered whether or not we were 
supposed to take off our shoes before going on board.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:39.930
There have been a lot of frightening times, but I was 
proud to be able to serve on the best ship in the world.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:47.110
In November 1944, when we finally returned 
home to Kure, I got injured and was discharged.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.860
About 4 months later, the Yamato sank.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.510
I regretted having to leave her before the end,

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:57.300
but I can still say I've served on the Yamato.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:00.810
That kind of pride helped support me.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.490
That photo is about as important as the other ones.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.480
I hope he gets well soon.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.720
You really like the elderly, don't you?

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.280
You have to be kind to your seniors.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.320
Besides, it's fun listening to their stories.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.410
Well, that's true.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.430
More fun than talking to girls?

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.120
Like your female classmates, for instance.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:34.800
Possibly.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:39.490
I don't know much about pop culture 
and such, so it wouldn't be fun for them.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:40.690
That's not true!

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.500
—I think.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.110
Thanks, Hitotsubashi-san.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:54.850
Come on, let's go home.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.130
Wait up!

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.010
I found you!

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.420
Good morning!

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:07.740
Good morning.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.330
You're up late.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.150
We all already finished eating breakfast.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.480
Who cares, it's Sunday.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:18.830
Clean up after you're done!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:19.800
Okay!

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:33.250
Let's eat!

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:33.800
Yurie-sama!

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:39.780
We finally meet!

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.490
My name is Mitsubamaru.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:45.070
I had a favor to ask, so I came all the way from Okinawa.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.200
Okinawa?

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.020
Yes!

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:53.180
Yurie-sama, please let Yamato-san go home!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:15.210
Yamato-san is currently on the bottom of the ocean 
in the East China Sea off the coast of Tokunoshima,

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.630
30.43 degrees northern latitude,

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:21.400
128.04 degrees eastern longitude, depth 344 meters.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:27.820
He's been there for a long time now, 
helping out us newly sunken ships.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.410
He is loved by everyone.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:35.690
But over the years he started talking about his past more,

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.280
especially about his birthplace, Kure.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.900
How nostalgic.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:46.120
I was travelling across Japan in that 
time until after the war as well.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.570
Have you been around that long, Bin-chan?

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.250
Well, yes—

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:56.690
Due to the period of strong economic growth 
afterwards, I had no place to go anymore.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.130
The olden days were great.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.530
I'm a ship too, so I can understand.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:07.400
Even if you live on the sea, you still 
want to return to port eventually.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.780
Yamato-san really wants to go back to Kure as well.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:18.450
That's why we asked the previous god in 
charge to at least let his spirit go back—

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.670
He wasn't able to get him back?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:28.420
That god was boastful about having Yamato-san 
in his own domain, so he wouldn't help us.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:33.450
But I realised from that typhoon awhile back 
that a new god had taken charge here—

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.080
Oh, that—

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:39.310
So I set off on a journey to ask you for help.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:43.470
I can jump from water to water 
if they are in close proximity.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:51.520
Then, it took you about 4 months to get here—?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.740
That's right—

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.320
It was horrible!

00:07:55.790 --> 00:08:02.070
I was drunk up by people, water froze while I 
was sleeping, I got drunk from jumping into sake!

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.150
Please, Yurie-sama.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.080
I really want to help you—

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.980
but I wonder what I should do?

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:17.700
What to do indeed—

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.100
When did you—?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.890
When there is a request to be 
fulfilled, we are there for you.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:25.730
Even so, you're trying to bring 
battleship Yamato-san back home.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.770
That's going to be difficult.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:33.870
Yurie-sama, I think you'll be able 
to grant Mitsubamaru-san's wish.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:34.700
Then?

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:38.780
But how about asking Yamato-san about his feelings first?

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.870
Yamato-san's feelings?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:46.610
Go ahead.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.490
Can I talk to him through this?

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:49.280
Yes.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:52.800
Um—

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:56.120
Hello, my name is Yurie.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.290
Is this Yamato-san?

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:02.460
Yes, Yamato here.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.190
I see—

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:10.100
Mitsubamaru-kun did something like that—

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.360
Just when I thought I hadn't 
seen him around lately—

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:14.960
Er—

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:19.500
So, do you want to go back, Yamato-san?

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.450
I will do anything I can to help you.

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:27.370
Please tell me what you honestly want.

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:31.990
I sometimes see Kure in my dreams.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:39.230
After all, it's the place I was born.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:40.660
So?

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:47.060
However, I'm too embarrassed 
to ever go back there now.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:52.020
Everyone made me so beautiful and sent me off,

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.360
I can't show my face anymore in this state.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:10:02.430
Because I've been here for so long, I've 
also forgotten the way I used to look like,

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:06.550
it would just be rude to everyone if such 
an unsightly spirit was to return there.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.290
There are people who need me down here as well,

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:15.260
so I think it may be for the best to 
stay here and dissolve in the ocean.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.000
You're not unsightly at all!

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:22.520
You became that way because you did your job!

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.000
No one is blaming you for that.

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:30.380
You are our hero, the pride of us ships!

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:35.460
Please be honest about your feelings!

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:41.520
Um—

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:42.870
Yamato-san?

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:47.970
Even now, there are a lot of 
people that still remember you.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:52.610
There are people who are proud 
that they were able to serve on you.

00:10:53.140 --> 00:11:00.010
I'm sure that whatever you want to 
do will make them happy as well.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:04.030
I'll do anything in my power to help you.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:08.290
Can I count on you?

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:14.270
I understand.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.610
Leave it to me!

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:17.780
Your request has been accepted!

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.790
It's going to be a rough ride—

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:24.110
Goodbye.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.040
Let's see—

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.170
To put it simply, it's not impossible to do.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.010
You're only returning his spirit.

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:38.800
You can help him if you tune in with his heart.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.050
That's good.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:46.140
So how do I "tune in" with him?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.600
For starters,

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:51.590
knowing everything there is to know about 
what kind of ship Yamato-san was is essential.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:57.500
Exterior, volume, width, weight, interior.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.070
The reasons it was constructed.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:03.860
If you know all of that, you can 
become closer to Yamato-san.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:05.180
I see.

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.480
I'll have to do research on Yamato-san right away!

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:15.270
Battleship Yamato.

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:17.880
1937: Laid down.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:20.890
What's "laid down"?

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:22.790
What are you doing?

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:26.320
Yamato?

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:28.660
The one from Gen-san's story?

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:29.350
Yeah.

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.310
Hey, help me out!

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:42.290
51, 52, 53, 154. This is about 100 meters!

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:44.210
Thanks!

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:46.020
What's Yamato's length?

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:49.190
263 meters.

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:51.880
That's about 2.6 times this length.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:55.310
It's just too big—

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:58.500
What's Yamato's capacity?

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.670
Around 3000 people.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:04.130
About 7 times our school.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:08.150
Yes, I would like to borrow some books about Yamato.

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:10.120
As many as possible.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:15.710
There are some that contain confidential 
information, but I guess we owe you one.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.740
I'll see to it.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:21.060
It's me.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.210
Put me through to the National Diet Library.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:27.540
Did you know?

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:31.240
There was a room inside Yamato 
where they made lemonade.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.660
You're kidding, right?

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:33.950
It's true!

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:38.570
They were to be handed out 
to the crew on long voyages.

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:39.840
You're lying.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:43.420
Sign: Lemonade here

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.600
It's the truth!

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:46.770
Really?

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.680
Really.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.970
Yurie-sama.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:53.650
What are you drawing?

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.770
Lemonade here

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.770
How's the resemblance?

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:01.180
Er, I don't really know—

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.770
<i>But this isn't really right, is it?</i>

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:07.950
Lemonade here

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:12.750
One, two—

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:36.810
I don't understand—

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.090
Yurie-chan!

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:51.710
This is 260 meters!

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.020
It's this big—

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.130
Do you have a rough image of it now?

00:14:59.130 --> 00:14:59.880
Yes.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:05.070
The problem now isn't the data, 
but the atmosphere on Yamato-san.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.710
It would be nice if there were 
someone who knew about it—

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:12.470
Then I know someone who can help us!

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:16.640
Sometimes, we had fishing days.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:21.450
We lined up on the deck with 200-300 men, 
and cast our fishing rods into the ocean.

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:23.920
We used nails as fish hooks and sardines as bait.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.860
It was quite a spectacle!

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:30.670
Since we were near the southern 
islands, squalls would often come in.

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:34.110
Whenever that happened, everyone came 
out buck naked with only a towel and soap,

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:36.470
and started washing their bodies!

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:40.080
It also happened that it stopped raining 
while everyone was still covered in foam!

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.100
That can't be a true story!

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.660
I've heard that one a hundred times!

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:48.670
That wasn't written in the documents.

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.550
They obviously don't put things like that in.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:56.070
But you know, even though the war 
was tiring, that was a great ship.

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:59.570
I believe that ship was worth spending my youth on.

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:04.520
I really want to see it again—

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:11.450
Well, I'm off.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.600
Okinawa, huh? How nice.

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.960
I'd like some souki soba as a souvenir.

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.560
It won't be like that—

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.400
Yurie-sama, go go!

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:21.760
Don't drown!

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:23.920
Please come back soon!

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:25.640
It's gonna be fine!

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.130
I think.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.330
Take care.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:29.420
I will.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.340
Let's go.

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.260
Ka—

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:41.520
mi—

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.280
chu!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.720
Hey, thinking about it—

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:56.490
What?

00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:00.210
Are there spirits around us right now as well?

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:01.620
There probably are.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:03.620
There are.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:15.510
Yurie-sama.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.550
Mitsubamaru-san!

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:21.010
So you were actually this great.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.880
I'm a ship as well, after all. Come, hop on!

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:36.820
Yurie-sama.

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.500
Yamato-san!

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:51.230
Good day, Yurie-sama.

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:53.940
Hello.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.780
Welcome back, Mitsubamaru-kun.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.010
I have returned!

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:02.350
You're so big—

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.500
Are you surprised?

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:07.950
Nope, I knew all about it!

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:27.680
I will now give the sign to take you up top.

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:30.770
Please focus on getting to the surface with me.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.590
Thank you for helping out.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.050
No obstacles on the surface detected.

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:48.660
Yamato, surfacing!

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:50.270
Surfacing!

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.850
Yamato, surfacing successful!

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:39.400
It's been a long time since I felt this breeze!

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:45.920
Yamato-san—

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:47.910
Thank you, Mitsubamaru-kun.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:49.330
Don't mention it!

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:54.580
Please watch over this sea in my place.

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:56.440
I can't!

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:58.220
I'm just a fishing boat!

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:01.700
I'm not as big and wonderful as you!

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:04.320
You are quite wonderful.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:10.160
You pursued your goal without 
giving up and returned here, after all.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.550
Wonderful!

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:15.000
You're looking great!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:15.930
It's all right!

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:16.570
Do your best!

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:17.720
I will!

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:22.820
Well then, Yurie-sama—

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:23.720
Okay.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:27.030
Destination: Kure, Hiroshima prefecture.

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:30.950
Yamato, return to base!

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:32.740
Roger!

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:46.600
Farewell, Yamato-san!

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:49.670
Thank you, from the bottom of my heart!

00:20:57.640 --> 00:21:00.620
I have one favor to ask of you though—

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:09.840
So you came too, huh?

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:11.160
Oh, Gen-san!

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:13.580
Yeah, Matsuri invited me.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:16.010
It wasn't me.

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:18.120
Yurie invited the two of you.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:19.840
She has something to show you.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:22.310
What's going to happen?

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:24.740
Are you okay?

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:25.960
Don't push yourself—

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:26.960
I'm fine!

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:30.780
Please take this.

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:40.530
Amazing—

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:42.230
What the heck—

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:46.660
Hey, did you feel that?

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:47.980
He's here!

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:58.080
I'm so excited!

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:19.930
Hey!

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:21.920
Hitotsubashi-san—

00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:25.690
What's that?

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:28.350
Yurie—

00:22:30.330 --> 00:22:32.280
Why are you laughing?

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:35.750
Sign: Lemonade here

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:39.210
Sorry, Yamato-san.

00:22:39.770 --> 00:22:42.600
I don't mind something like this on me.

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:43.860
That's good.

00:22:44.390 --> 00:22:46.640
That's Gen-san over there, isn't it?

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:50.860
I'm surprised you knew—

00:22:51.250 --> 00:22:56.030
Well, I still remember him, and 
he's synchronized with you as well.

00:22:56.920 --> 00:22:59.670
The boy beside him is the person you like, isn't he?

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:08.060
Yamato-san, those are confidential matters!

00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:25.000
How exciting!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.070
It reminds me of the olden days.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:32.370
Yamato, you really are the best ship in the world!

00:23:36.030 --> 00:23:38.180
Farewell, everyone.

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:43.560
Yamato, returning to base!

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:57.480
Hey, hand me the nails!

00:23:57.480 --> 00:23:58.100
Yes, sir!

00:23:58.740 --> 00:23:59.690
Gen-san!

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:02.260
Are you fine now?

00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:03.810
Of course!

00:24:03.810 --> 00:24:07.330
This roof is nothing compared to Yamato!

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:09.520
Well that's obvious, but—

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:12.180
Oh, Hitotsubashi-san?

00:24:14.070 --> 00:24:14.710
Yes?

00:24:15.110 --> 00:24:16.620
Thanks for the other day.

00:24:16.620 --> 00:24:18.790
Thanks to you I got to see something amazing.

00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:21.350
It'll be helpful for my calligraphy.

00:24:23.210 --> 00:24:24.510
It's no big deal—

00:24:24.510 --> 00:24:26.830
Are you two dating or something?

00:24:29.930 --> 00:24:32.110
Nope, we're just friends!

00:24:32.700 --> 00:24:33.920
That's what I figured.

00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:35.960
To a man, work is more important than women.

00:24:35.960 --> 00:24:37.140
Come on, give me a plank.

00:24:37.140 --> 00:24:37.660
Yes, sir!

00:24:38.970 --> 00:24:41.990
Petite warship Yurie, report current status.

00:24:42.420 --> 00:24:45.550
Currently sinking in deep silence, over.

00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:55.750
<b>mada mada zenzen owannai last ichijikan no jugyou desu</b>

00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:55.750
<b>The last class of the day never seems to end</b>

00:24:55.750 --> 00:25:00.620
<b>tokei wo chira chira mitemo ichi byou ga nagai ne</b>

00:24:55.750 --> 00:25:00.620
<b>Even if I keep glancing at my watch, a second seems an eternity</b>

00:25:01.640 --> 00:25:07.690
<b>mabushii koutei mieru kimi no hashiru sugata oikake</b>

00:25:01.640 --> 00:25:07.690
<b>In the radiant schoolyard, trailing your running visage,</b>

00:25:07.690 --> 00:25:12.830
<b>houkago love-love date mousou shite bosou chuu</b>

00:25:07.690 --> 00:25:12.830
<b>my imagination is running wild about our date after class</b>

00:25:13.720 --> 00:25:16.740
<b>chime no kane koi no signal</b>

00:25:13.720 --> 00:25:16.740
<b>The school chimes ring and it's a signal of love!</b>

00:25:16.740 --> 00:25:19.740
<b>rouka no tobidashi ni wa chuui</b>

00:25:16.740 --> 00:25:19.740
<b>Be careful if you rush out into the hallway!</b>

00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:22.710
<b>kimi no moto e ichiban saki ni</b>

00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:22.710
<b>I dash to see you, first thing!</b>

00:25:22.710 --> 00:25:25.330
<b>issho ni kaerou</b>

00:25:22.710 --> 00:25:25.330
<b>Let's go home together!</b>

00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:32.970
<b>soda aji no ice candy gira gira na ohisama no shita hanbunko</b>

00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:32.970
<b>Sharing a soda-flavored popsicle under the glaring sun</b>

00:25:32.970 --> 00:25:39.010
<b>torokesou na atashi no seishun desu doki doki shichau</b>

00:25:32.970 --> 00:25:39.010
<b>My youth seems to melt with it, it makes my heart beat faster</b>

00:25:39.010 --> 00:25:44.460
<b>kono nanigenai toki wo ima mune ni shimatte</b>

00:25:39.010 --> 00:25:44.460
<b>I'm shutting our casual time in my heart</b>

00:25:44.760 --> 00:25:51.890
<b>asu wa mata kyou yori mo kimi wo suki ni naru no desu</b>

00:25:44.760 --> 00:25:51.890
<b>Tomorrow I will love you even more than today</b>

00:25:56.040 --> 00:26:11.040
<b>Preview</b>

00:25:56.280 --> 00:26:00.120
I'm Hitotsubashi Yurie, running 
for student council presidency!

00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:05.040
If I get elected, I'll do my best to 
create a cheerful, carefree school!

00:26:05.620 --> 00:26:07.870
Next episode, You Decide.

00:26:05.960 --> 00:26:11.040
<b>You Decide</b>

00:26:07.870 --> 00:26:10.170
Please give me your attention!
